What:           /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/pending_version_depth
Date:           September 2026
KernelVersion:  7.1 CJFS research fork
Description:
                Root-only staged shadow-version slot depth, integer 1..5.
                Default 1. Changes take effect only upon successful apply.

What:           /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/pending_copy_mode
Date:           September 2026
KernelVersion:  7.1 CJFS research fork
Description:
                Root-only staged copy policy: lazy (default) or eager.
                Required escaping/undo copies are unaffected.

What:           /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/pending_coalesce_us
Date:           September 2026
KernelVersion:  7.1 CJFS research fork
Description:
                Root-only staged conflict coalescing budget, 0..10000 us.
                Default 0 disables optional coalescing. The budget is not
                renewed on retry and does not bound mandatory conflict waits.

What:           /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/apply
Date:           September 2026
KernelVersion:  7.1 CJFS research fork
Description:
                Root-only write of 1 drains the journal while blocking new
                ordinary handles, then atomically publishes the pending tuple
                and increments generation. It always releases its admission
                barrier before returning. Failed drains preserve active values.
                Requires writable, unfrozen ordered-data ext4 with an internal
                journal and Fast Commit inactive. Competing userspace controllers
                must serialize the entire stage/apply/readback sequence.

What:           /sys/fs/ext4/<device>/cjfs/effective
Date:           September 2026
KernelVersion:  7.1 CJFS research fork
Description:
                Root-only read returns a coherent line:
                depth copy_mode coalesce_us generation
                Generation starts at 1 for each newly created journal instance.
